 # Preview Specifications
 
+## Request Handling
+
 - [ ] **PREVIEW-001**: When a request identifies an unknown clip revision, the system SHALL return 404 without enqueuing a render job.
-- [ ] **PREVIEW-002**: When the requested preview is cached, the system SHALL return 200 with the JPEG for the requested revision and renderer version.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-002**: When the requested preview is cached and accessible, the system SHALL return 200 with the JPEG for the requested revision and renderer version.
 - [ ] **PREVIEW-003**: When concurrent requests miss the cache for the same preview key, the system SHALL return 202 with the same job ticket and a two-second retry interval while one shared render job is pending.
-- [ ] **PREVIEW-004**: When admitting a completed preview would exceed 12 GiB of cached JPEG data, the system SHALL evict entries before admission so the cache remains within that limit.
 - [ ] **PREVIEW-005**: When a render job fails, the system SHALL release its deduplication entry so a later request can enqueue a new job.
+
+## Cache Management and Eviction
+
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-004**: When admitting a completed preview would exceed 12 GiB of cached JPEG data, the system SHALL evict entries before admission so the cache remains within that limit.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-006**: The cache SHALL maintain two separate queues: A1 (first-use entries, sized at 1/4 of total capacity = 3 GiB) and Am (reused/active entries, using remaining capacity).
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-007**: When a request hits an entry in the A1 queue, the system SHALL promote that entry to the Am queue.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-008**: When a cache miss occurs and the entry would be inserted, the system SHALL place new entries directly into A1 if they fit within A1's size limit, otherwise directly into Am.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-009**: When A1 exceeds its 3 GiB capacity, the system SHALL evict the oldest entry from A1 without adding it to Am.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-010**: When Am requires eviction to stay within the 9 GiB available capacity, the system SHALL evict entries using least-recently-used (LRU) order within Am.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-011**: Eviction metadata (queue membership, access order, size tracking) SHALL remain private to the preview worker and never expose queue state to callers or other subsystems.
